From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Darrel=20Gri=C3=ABt?= <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 23:19:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] misc: bq5105x_detect: Don't force the backlight on the
 wireless dock
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

bq5105x_detect broadcasts DISPLAY_WAKE_EVENT_DOCKON when the dock is
detected. While docked, m4sensorhub_als then sends its light readings
to leds-lm3535 instead of userspace.

The hwcomposer plugin calls the power HAL's setInteractive(false) after
turning the screen off. power.minnow.so writes that to lm3535's
"interactive" node. lm3535 then turns the backlight back on at a level
derived from each reading. The backlight stays lit with the screen off.

Drop the broadcast. m4sensorhub_als then keeps sending its readings to
userspace, resulting in the backlight staying off while docked.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AsteroidOS-specific policy]
Signed-off-by: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c b/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c
index 37cbdcaa11ce..b8889b551622 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c
@@ -215,11 +215,6 @@ static void bq5105x_detect_report(struct bq5105x_detect *chip, bool docked)
 {
 	if (chip->reported_docked != docked) {
 		dev_dbg(&chip->pdev->dev, "report docked=%d\n", docked);
-#ifdef CONFIG_WAKEUP_SOURCE_NOTIFY
-		wakeup_source_notify_subscriber(docked
-						? DISPLAY_WAKE_EVENT_DOCKON
-						: DISPLAY_WAKE_EVENT_DOCKOFF);
-#endif
 		chip->reported_docked = docked;
 		power_supply_changed(&chip->charger);
 		switch_set_state(chip->sdev, docked);
-- 
